1. Memory safety issues
    Improper management of memory allocation, access, and deallocation.
    120 - buffer overflow
    125 - out-of-bounds released
    416 - user-after-free
    Typical impact: System crashes (DoS), Arbitrary Code Execution (RCE), Information leakage

2. Injection flaws
    Untrusted data is sent to an interpreter as part of a command or query.
    79 - XSS
    89 - SQL Injection
    78 - command Injection
    Typical impact: Data loss, corruption, unauthorized access, full system takeover

3. Authentication & Access Control Issues
    Broken identity or permission enforcement.
    287 - Improper Authentication
    862 - Missing Authorization
    522 - Insufficiently Protected Credentials
    Typical impact: Privilege escalation, Unauthorized data access

4. Cryptographic Failures
    Weak or misused cryptography.
    327 - Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm
    326 - Inadequate Encryption Strength
    295 - Improper Certificate Validation
    Typical impact: Data exposure, Man-in-the-middle attacks

5. Configuration & Deployment Issues
    Insecure defaults or misconfigurations.
    16  - Configuration (Category)
    276 - Incorrect Default Permissions
    1188 - Insecure Default Initialization of Resource
    Typical impact: Exposure of internal systems, Privilege abuse

6. Input Validation & Data Handling Errors
    Failure to properly validate or sanitize data.
    20  - Improper Input Validation
    190 - Integer Overflow or Wraparound
    22  - Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')
    Typical impact: Data corruption, RCE, File disclosure

7. Race Conditions & Concurrency Issues
    Timing-related logic flaws.
    362 - Concurrent Execution using Shared Resource with Improper Synchronization ('Race Condition')
    367 - Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition
    Typical impact: Privilege escalation, Data corruption
